---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const updated = '2026-08-23';
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
const blogHost = site.links.blog.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');
const notesHost = site.links.notes.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');
---

<Layout background="mountains"
  heading="Legal"
  description={`AI disclosure, copyright, privacy, and disclaimers for ${site.name}'s sites`}
>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-[40rem] text-lede text-muted">
    AI disclosure, copyright, privacy, and disclaimers for this site, <a href={site.links.blog}>{blogHost}</a>, and{' '}
    <a href={site.links.notes}>{notesHost}</a>. Last updated {updated}.
  </p>

  <Section title="AI disclosure">
    <div class="max-w-[40rem] space-y-4">
      <p>
        The writing on these sites reflects my own ideas and opinions. I draft and edit with generative AI assistance —
        currently Anthropic's Claude models — including source research, and I review everything before it is
        published. Nothing goes out without that review.
      </p>
      <p>
        Blog posts carry a notice at the top naming the model that helped. Notes are drafted, edited, and organized
        with the same tools; clipped third-party articles there are marked as such and remain the work of their
        original authors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Code for this site and for my public repositories on <a href={site.links.github}>GitHub</a> is written with
        AI coding assistants. It is reviewed and tested before it is merged, and each repository's history records
        what changed and when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Copyright">
    <div class="max-w-[40rem] space-y-4">
      <p>
        Unless stated otherwise, the content on these sites is © {year} {site.name}. All rights reserved. Short
        quotations with attribution and a link back are welcome.
      </p>
      <p>
        Code in my public repositories is licensed under the license file that accompanies each repository. Quoted and
        clipped third-party material belongs to its original authors and is reproduced for reference with attribution.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Privacy">
    <div class="max-w-[40rem] space-y-4">
      <p>
        These are static sites with no accounts and no forms that accept input. This site and the blog set no cookies
        and load no analytics, advertising, or tracking scripts. The notes site loads
        <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible</a>, a
        cookieless analytics script that counts page views in aggregate without storing personal identifiers or
        tracking you across sites, and serves its web fonts from Google Fonts, which sees your IP address when the
        fonts load.
      </p>
      <p>
        The sites are hosted on Amazon Web Services in the United States (S3, CloudFront, Route 53, and AWS WAF). To
        serve pages and block abuse, AWS processes standard request metadata — IP address, user agent, and the URL
        requested — and applies security rules that block traffic from sanctioned countries, rate-limit individual
        addresses, and reject known-malicious IPs. I do not enable access logging; AWS may retain sampled request
        metadata briefly for security monitoring under the
        <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AWS Privacy Notice</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links to other sites lead to services with their own privacy practices. If you contact me directly, I keep the
        correspondence only as long as needed to respond.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Disclaimers">
    <div class="max-w-[40rem] space-y-4">
      <p>
        This is a personal site. The views here are my own and do not represent any employer, client, or other
        organization, past or present.
      </p>
      <p>
        Content is provided for general information, as is, without warranty of any kind. It is not legal, financial,
        security, or other professional advice. Technical guidance ages quickly; verify it against current
        documentation before relying on it in production.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Amazon Web Services, Anthropic, GitHub, or any other
        vendor mentioned. Product names and trademarks belong to their owners. There is no sponsored, affiliate, or
        paid content on these sites; if that changes, it will be disclosed where it appears.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Contact">
    <div class="max-w-[40rem] space-y-4">
      <p>
        For questions about this page, corrections, attribution, or a request to remove material you hold rights to,
        reach me on <a href={site.links.github}>GitHub</a>. I will respond promptly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Changes">
    <div class="max-w-[40rem] space-y-4">
      <p>
        This page will change as the sites and the tools behind them change. The date at the top is the last revision;
        the <a href="https://github.com/rwaterman/website">site repository</a> holds the full history.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>
